Essentially there are `n' PICs or read points on the cpu where you can load an event to monitor and monitors its results. Its 
not like ours where you can load lots of signals and get them dumped from memory.

So in this case we loaded 4 signals on 4 separate PICs to monitor.

Oh and btw before you load an event on PIC make sure via cputrack -h that event is actually supported on the PIC.
